# The literal's two closures are made when they are read: its slots hold a mark, and code that reads such a slot typed names the function.
# The front end expects the literal in `drive`, by the names asked there. Nothing of the program brings it there, so nothing in Link leads from `drive` to `next`:
# the build stopped by its own net ("the code of function 1 'drive' .. mentions function 4 'next' .. and LinkTables::referrers does not lead from the one to the other").
# Where the unit may not mention the function, the read goes by name.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK-NOT: GetDeferredClosureSlot
# RUN(PLAN): plan layouts mechanisms=all
# PLAN: "next" DeferredClosure
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 6 0123 0123
# ANSWERS-NEXT: exited with 0
